{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/847983-does-mummy-have-a-metaplot","id":847983,"title":"Does Mummy have a Metaplot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-15T20:29:13-07:00","id":847983,"title":"Does Mummy have a Metaplot?","content":"As the title says, I'm wondering if Mummy has a metaplot. I've heard it does and that it leans a lot on very specific fluff that storytellers know and the player might eventually discover. But that sounds weird for a Chronicles of Darkness game since I thought the metaplot stuff was just oWoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:43:03-07:00","id":847986,"title":"","content":"Th old metaplot was defined by events progressing as supplements came out, an overarching story told across releases sharing characters that impacted the game world.<br /> <br /> Mummy has nothing like this. It has a backstory that's been rather significantly added to, and a handful of NPCs are recurring as footnotes in history, but they're just that; footnotes with largely irrelevent names attached to them. While there's more fluff now than there was back when it was just the corebook, the additions do not have any major effect on things as a whole, largely because they've all been added to a history that's almost entirely forgotten by the player characters. The confusion arises from Mummy having a comparatively demser background than the other CofD games; the Nameless Empire and the Arisen have a lot more told about them as 'true' than, say, an individual Vampire covenant or Wereolf tribe.<br /> <br /> That's before you factor in the toolkit approach of the CofD; it's up to individual Storyteller's to explain what the Deceived are like in their home chronicle, or what happened during the Second Turn, and the average chronicle will never cross paths with The Heretic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:59:21-07:00","id":847991,"title":"","content":"As atamajakki says, it's not that it has a metaplot, but that it has much firmer &quot;canon&quot; than other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T22:27:13-07:00","id":848018,"title":"","content":"No metaplot. It has a backstory and default chronicle series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T23:51:55-07:00","id":848026,"title":"","content":"To better summarize:<br /> <br /> In Vampire, vampires come from somewhere. Each clan has several contradictory origin stories, further muddied by conflicting legends from the covenants and regional influences. The Kindred across the globe have no consensus, and there is no &quot;canon&quot; or &quot;true&quot; answer.<br /> <br /> In Mummy, the Arisen very definitely come from the Nameless Empire, a predynastic Egyptian civilization that prayed to the 42 Judges, believed in the five-fold heart, and served the necromancer-kings known as the Shan'iatu. There's no confusion about anynof this, and having such concrete answersvis what throws people off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-16-2016, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:56:00-07:00","id":848234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/847983-does-mummy-have-a-metaplot?p=847986#post847986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Th old metaplot was defined by events progressing as supplements came out, an overarching story told across releases sharing characters that impacted the game world.<br /> <br /> Mummy has nothing like this. It has a backstory that's been rather significantly added to, and a handful of NPCs are recurring as footnotes in history, but they're just that; footnotes with largely irrelevent names attached to them. While there's more fluff now than there was back when it was just the corebook, the additions do not have any major effect on things as a whole, largely because they've all been added to a history that's almost entirely forgotten by the player characters. The confusion arises from Mummy having a comparatively demser background than the other CofD games; the Nameless Empire and the Arisen have a lot more told about them as 'true' than, say, an individual Vampire covenant or Wereolf tribe.<br /> <br /> That's before you factor in the toolkit approach of the CofD; it's up to individual Storyteller's to explain what the Deceived are like in their home chronicle, or what happened during the Second Turn, and the average chronicle will never cross paths with The Heretic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, you beat me to it this time. Who does reoccur across several books, besides the Heretic? My brain is mush right now.","signature":"<h